WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- [Kelly] I mean, you're bringing

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.120
a little country with that dress,

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:02.953
(Julia chuckles)
I like it, I like it.

00:00:02.953 --> 00:00:04.200
- Thank you.
- Have y'all met before?

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.033
- No.
- No.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:05.866
- It's so lovely to meet you.

00:00:05.866 --> 00:00:08.040
- Oh, great to meet
you, I liked your show.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.101
- Thank you.

00:00:09.101 --> 00:00:10.544
(Kelly laughs)
I liked your shows too.

00:00:10.544 --> 00:00:11.377
(Julia laughs)
- Thanks, thanks.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:13.112
- [Kelly] I think a few have watched, Lisa

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.151
- A few, just a few.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:14.151 --> 00:00:17.270
- So, do your kids express
interest in learning about,

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.240
you know, the Orthodox Jews,
do they express anything?

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.740
- Well, they all lived in
that community with me.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.910
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.250
- Right, my daughter was
already married when I left.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.378
So, they know enough.

00:00:25.378 --> 00:00:26.700
- [Kelly] So, have they talked
about it at all, though?

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.965
Like the switch.

00:00:27.965 --> 00:00:29.670
- [Julia] You know, to them...

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.630
- [Kelly] I guess why
I'm saying this is like,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.240
even with like, divorce with my family,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.550
like my kids, I feel like
we've talked about it enough

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:35.920
and then it'll just come back up again.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.692
And I'm like, "Oh, we're revisiting it".

00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:38.750
(audience laughs)
So, yeah.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.370
- I think they're just very grateful

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.740
for the life that we have now.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.730
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.020
- And that they get to
make their own choices

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.661
and that their biology
doesn't define their destiny.

00:00:46.661 --> 00:00:47.494
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:47.494 --> 00:00:48.820
- So, I think they,

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.050
they know the beauty of
the world we came from,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.320
but they also understand why we left.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.153
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.736
Well, that's important.
(audience applauds)

00:00:55.736 --> 00:00:58.420
What impresses your kids the most?

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.650
Like, you taking risks in your life

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.168
or you knowing Kendall Jenner?

00:01:02.168 --> 00:01:03.010
(Julia and audience laughs)

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:03.843
What is the big thing?

00:01:03.843 --> 00:01:05.510
- Well, I think it's that, you know,

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:07.967
I left a world, you know I always say,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.800
"I'm a time traveler".

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.990
I left the 1800's and I came to...

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.110
Because I mean, that's kind
of, the world I lived in.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:14.943
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:14.943 --> 00:01:18.307
- Women got married, they
had babies when they were 19.

00:01:18.307 --> 00:01:19.140
They're supposed to be,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.720
you know, obedient to their husbands.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.550
It was a very different kind of world.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.150
And then, I came into this world,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.000
without a college education,
without knowing anything

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.950
and then I started a shoe brand.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.750
So, I think for them,

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.640
it's that time travel journey.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.280
The fact that I, at 42 years old,

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.750
picked myself up and
started an entire new life.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.583
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:40.700
- That, you know, I think that's the thing

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.810
that they appreciate the most.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:42.910
- [Kelly] Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:43.743
- [Julia] Yeah.

00:01:43.743 --> 00:01:44.634
- It was a joke, the Kendall thing.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:45.500
(audience applauds)
(Julia laughs)

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.240
But speaking of, the
reason why I brought it up,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.450
is because this is a shot of the gown

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.650
that you made her for the Met Gala.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.590
So, I want to show,
this is a few years ago.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.423
- [Lisa] Wow.
(audience gasps)

00:01:54.423 --> 00:01:55.840
- [Kelly] Like, oh.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.380
I mean, first of all, were we
supposed to look like that?

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.650
Like, I don't understand
what's happening there.

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.370
But like, I mean, that is beautiful

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.210
and how is that held together?

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.043
- Oh, my gosh.

00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:05.876
- I feel like its delicate.

00:02:05.876 --> 00:02:06.990
- Oh my God, no, you have no idea.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.140
Literally, I had total nightmares,

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.820
because I wanted to make a
dress that had no fabric.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:17.100
It's just thread and 85,000 crystals.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:17.970
- Wow.
- What?

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.770
- And the problem though...

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:23.360
- I love that you wanted to
make a dress with no fabric.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.783
I just have to stop there for a minute.

00:02:24.783 --> 00:02:25.950
(Kelly laughs)
That was your idea.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.350
I had a dream and...
- Wow.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.183
- No fabric needed.

00:02:29.183 --> 00:02:31.460
- Because you know, it's
about thinking out of the box.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.330
- I love it, it's beautiful.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.300
- So, my only fear is

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.300
you see how like, it on the bottom there,

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.390
it kind of falls on the ground.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.800
I was petrified.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.760
- [Kelly] Ooh, someone would step on it.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.593
- [Julia] Yes.

00:02:41.593 --> 00:02:42.430
- [Kelly] That's happened to me.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.263
- [Julia] I mean, imagine,

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.060
because if you step on somebody's dress...

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:45.893
- [Kelly] And it rips.

00:02:45.893 --> 00:02:46.726
- And it rips.

00:02:46.726 --> 00:02:48.160
If someone stepped on her dress.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:48.993
- [Kelly] Oh, no.

00:02:48.993 --> 00:02:52.390
- 85,000 crystals would come crashing down

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.090
and she would be...

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:54.980
- In the buff.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.120
Yeah, just as Eve was.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.766
- [Julia] And so, that
was my literal panic.

00:02:59.766 --> 00:03:01.900
- I wanted to have like,
security guards around her

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.820
so that no one would be able
to go anywhere near the dress.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.210
- And people always step on your dress,

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.060
or maybe it's just me.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:07.893
I feel like people always...

00:03:07.893 --> 00:03:09.199
- [Lisa] They do.
- Yeah.

00:03:09.199 --> 00:03:10.032
- They do.
- They do.

00:03:10.032 --> 00:03:12.759
- I know, anytime I see a
train, I'm like, "I am screwed".

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:13.667
(audience laughs)

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:14.500
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.333
They're going to, it's going to happen.

00:03:15.333 --> 00:03:16.166
- And I was at the Met Gala.

00:03:16.166 --> 00:03:17.210
- But Julia, it could
have been tea length.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.510
- [Kelly] Tea length.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.240
- [Julia] I always make
life difficult for myself.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.170
This is what I do, I don't know.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.620
- It was so beautiful, though.
- Thank you.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.009
- I love that you thought
outside of the box.

00:03:24.009 --> 00:03:24.842
- Thank you.

00:03:24.842 --> 00:03:25.675
- I think that was really cool.

00:03:25.675 --> 00:03:26.508
- It was really fun.

00:03:26.508 --> 00:03:28.349
- So, the new book, so
this is called "Brazen".

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:29.182
- [Lisa] Oh, my gosh.

00:03:29.182 --> 00:03:30.970
- I know, it's very fancy.
- Wow.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.170
- So, it's an autobiography.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.400
So, it's called "Brazen".

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.570
So, why did you want to write this?

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.180
Why did you feel like it was important?

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.830
- Well, you know, I've been
through quite an unusual journey

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.800
and even through the TV show,

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.867
people would say to me,

00:03:43.867 --> 00:03:47.900
"Because I watched your
show, I left a bad marriage,

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.300
I started my business".

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.750
I had two people tell me this,

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.380
they had been planning to commit suicide.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:54.280
- Oh, wow.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.370
- And after they saw
the show, they didn't.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.820
So to me, the book,

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.320
because this show was
about my current life,

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.280
informed by my past.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.700
The book tells my whole, crazy journey.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.910
And it's a mess.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:09.428
And I'm very honest, because
I made a lot of mistakes,

00:04:09.428 --> 00:04:10.261
because I didn't know any better.

00:04:10.261 --> 00:04:11.170
- I think we all have, yeah.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.340
- You know, but I want people to know

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:15.030
that the mistakes are
part of the journey too.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.240
And that they shouldn't be
afraid to make mistakes,

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.280
they shouldn't be afraid
to try new things.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.570
So, I'm hoping that this
book inspires people,

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.388
gives people the courage to...

00:04:24.388 --> 00:04:25.221
- [Kelly] Helps people, yeah.

00:04:25.221 --> 00:04:26.840
- Yeah, gives people the courage to get up

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.170
and demand what they want from life

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:33.660
and not be held down by
people or others telling you

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.080
that you cannot or society,

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.440
whatever it is that's holding you back.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:42.067
I'm, really, I pray that
people read this book and say,

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:45.708
"Hey, if this crazy lady
can do it, so can I".

00:04:45.708 --> 00:04:46.541
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:46.541 --> 00:04:49.158
(audience applauds)

00:04:49.158 --> 00:04:51.020
- I feel like it would be hard for us

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.750
to find anyone in life that
doesn't have a messy path.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.167
We all have like, messes, you know?

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:56.210
- Of course.
- Yeah.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.043
- And I was so clueless.

00:04:57.043 --> 00:04:58.120
- It's if you wallow in it

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.953
or you pick it up and keep going.

